  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Department of Health and Human Services has obligated $14.3B on federal contracts in FY2026 to date. These obligations come from 21,023 awards, with an average award size of $680K, and obligations fell 32.9% year over year. The FY26 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure; prior full-year totals were $34.3B in FY21, $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, and $21.3B in FY25. Contracting remains concentrated in IT and professional services: Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $2.4B and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Consulting and custom programming also rank high, with Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $1.2B and Custom Computer Programming Services at $1B. The top vendors in FY2026 to date include GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $733M and MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M, followed by a mix of contractors providing IT, consulting, healthcare, and research services. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have HHS contract obligations changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 32.9% year over year. Full-year obligations were $34.3B in FY21, $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, and $21.3B in FY25, with $14.3B in FY26 to date. The FY26 number is a partial fiscal year total. The drop shows lower obligations in the current fiscal year to date relative to recent full years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is HHS buying and who is getting the work in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "HHS is buying mostly IT and professional services, with $2.4B in Computer Systems Design Services, $1.2B in Other Computer Related Services, $1.2B in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services, and $1B in Custom Computer Programming Services. Research and health categories also appear, including $837M for Biotechnology R&D and $827M for Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences R&D. The top vendors are led by GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $733M and MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M, followed by a mix of consulting and healthcare contractors."
      }
    ]
